# A method's own named Structure (OPUS-Q54-CONTINUE-20260929-14 2b): `S:` + fields in a method body, S resolving to
# nothing there, declares S by the general route (book §9: an absent target with an explicit Structure value), its type
# the Structure on the right.  At run time only that source-declared Structure exists: the statement builds it, a
# child of the method's own Structure, and binds it at S's own slot; S\v and S\w go through that slot.  7 when the
# write w: v + 3 reads back.  (It was refused: "unknown method" at its first field.)
fn: m () int
    S:
        size_t: v 4U
        size_t: w 5U
    S\w: S\v + 3U
    int: r 0
    if: S\w = 7U
        r: 7
    return: r
end: m
int: r 0
r: m()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
